{"title":"Career Roadmap · Clinical Physiotherapist","role":"Clinical Physiotherapist","summary":"A Clinical Physiotherapist assesses, treats, and monitors patients with movement, pain, physical-function, and mobility problems. The role combines clinical assessment, therapeutic exercise, rehabilitation techniques, patient education, and functional outcome measurement.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Physiotherapy (BPT)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Physiotherapist assesses, treats, and monitors patients with movement, pain, physical-function, and mobility problems. The role combines clinical assessment, therapeutic exercise, rehabilitation techniques, patient education, and functional outcome measurement."},{"type":"p","text":"For this pathway, BPT + supervised clinical internship + appropriate professional registration/licensing requirements form the core foundation. Postgraduate specialization is not mandatory for every clinical role, but MPT or a relevant master's degree can strengthen opportunities in specialist practice, teaching, research, and advanced clinical positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"BPT fundamentals, anatomy, physiology, biomechanics, exercise therapy and clinical skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2034"},{"text":"Clinical internship → Junior/Clinical Physiotherapist → broad patient exposure"}],[{"text":"2034–2040"},{"text":"Specialty clinical practice → advanced assessment → evidence-based rehabilitation"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Clinical Physiotherapist → Clinical Specialist → Team/Program Lead or advanced practice"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During BPT","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 